## Actual Behavior

TODO: Describe actual behavior

Found by lane-unused while fixing B088 (merged 2026-08-31). **Reported rather
than silently fixed**, on coordinator instruction, because the correct fix
changes behaviour for cases B088 did not touch.

## Defect

`complete_namespace_members` (`src/server/completion.rs:89`) emits EVERY member
it returns as `CompletionItemKind::FUNCTION` — nested namespaces and types
included. An editor therefore shows a namespace and a class with a function
icon.

Enum values are correct (`ENUM_MEMBER`) — B088 added those through a separate
path that knows what it is emitting.

## Why it was not fixed in B088

`TypeIndex::source_scope_members` returns **bare names with no kind**, so the
caller has nothing to key on. Fixing it properly means changing that function's
return type to carry a kind per member — which is a visible change to namespace
and type completion, i.e. exactly the cases B088 left alone. Widening a ticket
to cover them would have mixed a measured fix with an unmeasured one.

A code comment at the site records this, so the next reader finds the reason
rather than the symptom.

## Work

Change `source_scope_members` to return `(name, kind)` — it already
distinguishes its three sources internally (`source_names`, `functions`,
`scopes`), so the information exists at the point of collection and is
discarded on the way out. That is the whole defect: a lossy return type.

## Test plan

Assert the KIND, not just the presence, for each member class a real scope
yields: a nested namespace, a class, an enum type, a funcdef, and a function.
Generalise per CLAUDE.md — a Core namespace, a Nadeo class scope, and a
workspace namespace reach `source_scope_members` by different routes.

Include a control that the SET of names is unchanged, so a kind-carrying
refactor cannot quietly drop or add a member. That is the B080 lesson: when a
refactor changes a type, prove the values are the same before believing the
change was mechanical.

## Related

B088 (which added correct `ENUM_MEMBER` kinds and surfaced this), B069 (an
earlier completion defect where the wrong thing was offered).